# vehje-runtime-gen. backlog

Designed but deferred. Names stay unbackticked until they ship.

## The full lens-projection handoff

The handoff ships in its content-addressed manifest-check interim: the manifest
binds the package to the runtime and the differential harness checks the
projection. The full one-source-two-projections lens (the Rust compile-side
typestate and the Zig runtime consts both generated projections of the one
signature, differential-checked structurally rather than by manifest hash) is
the open handoff-staging question and lands here when it lands.

## The stencil section producer

The package schema reserves the copy-and-patch stencil section from day one, but
its producer is the deferred stencil toolchain (a dev-tool crate, weeks of
object-format work, never shipped to a consumer). This crate already owns the
manifest-hash binding of stencils to the semantic-definition hash (the novel
piece); the toolchain is a future producer of bytes for a slot that already
exists.

## Deepdive owed

A deepdive on runtime generation (the three loci, the manifest as the
no-trusted-emitter mechanism, the Deegen-style triple emission of interpreter
arm, value-kind, and stencil per operation) lands with the first real language
package.
